        "SCB-MANIFEST-003",
        "SCB-MANIFEST-004",
        "SCB-MANIFEST-005",
        "SCB-MANIFEST-006"
      ],
      "reason": "Boundary inventory, crate cycles and forbidden crate edges for the atm-core workspace. SCB-BOUNDARY-004 remains non-failing until randlee/sc-lint#642 fixes the published composition-root direction false positives."
    },
    "portability": {
      "config_home_env": "ATM_CONFIG_HOME",
      "enabled": true,
      "exclude_paths_by_rule": {
        "PORT-006": [
          "crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/peer_launch_config.rs"
        ],
        "PORT-007": [
          "crates/atm-core/src/doctor/herdr_state.rs",
          "crates/atm-herdr/src/transport.rs",
          "crates/atm-herdr/src/transport_socket.rs"
        ],
        "PORT-008": [
          "crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/peer_launch_config.rs"
        ],
        "PORT-010": [
          "crates/atm-core/src/atm_temp.rs",
          "crates/atm-core/src/atm_temp_sweeper.rs",
          "crates/atm-core/src/descriptor_limit.rs",
          "crates/atm-core/src/persistence.rs",
          "crates/atm-core/src/transfer_script.rs",
          "crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/lib.rs",
          "crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/protected_trust_root.rs",
          "crates/atm-daemon-client/src/lib.rs",
          "crates/atm-herdr/src/transport_socket.rs",
          "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/client.rs",
          "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/client_tail.rs",
          "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/http1_server.rs",
          "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/lib.rs",
          "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/loopback_tcp.rs",
          "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/runtime_listener.rs",
          "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/runtime_setup.rs",
          "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/unix_socket.rs",
          "crates/atm/src/main.rs"
        ]
      },
      "reason": "No analyzer-wide portability exclusion remains; each exception below is rule-scoped. PORT-007 (Windows named-pipe/verbatim path literals in Windows-only transport code): crates/atm-core/src/doctor/herdr_state.rs, crates/atm-herdr/src/transport.rs and crates/atm-herdr/src/transport_socket.rs, until randlee/sc-lint#192 adds reviewed-literal suppression. PORT-010 (production #[cfg(unix)] helpers with no same-scope #[cfg(windows)] sibling; their Windows behavior lives in a different module or is intentionally absent, and sc-lint 0.8.0 platform_adapters can pair only out-of-line #[cfg(unix)]/#[cfg(windows)] modules, of which atm-core has one unpaired cfg(unix) module, atm-http-runtime unix_socket, whose Windows counterpart loopback_tcp.rs is not a cfg(windows) module): every PORT-010 path listed, including crates/atm-http-runtime/src/loopback_tcp.rs and crates/atm-herdr/src/transport_socket.rs connect_unix, until randlee/sc-lint#372 ships. PORT-006 (/var/tmp/atm-ports under cfg(target_os = \"linux\")) and PORT-008 (USER with USERNAME fallback for the claim-owner label) in crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/peer_launch_config.rs: develop-sync baseline atm-phase-bg.sync-port-f1; the analyzer does not recognize target_os gating or the fallback, until randlee/sc-lint#641 ships.",
      "targets": [
        "linux",
        "macos",
        "windows"
      ],
      "unix_path_prefixes": [
        "/tmp/",
        "/home/",
        "/usr/",
        "/etc/"
      ]
    },
    "runtime": {
      "enabled": true,
      "exclude_paths_by_rule": {
        "SCB-RUNTIME-003": [
          "crates/atm/src/commands/internal_nudge.rs",
          "crates/atm-daemon-client/src/lib.rs"
        ]
      },
      "reason": "SCB-RUNTIME-003: internal_nudge.rs tmux delays and subprocess polling run on spawn_blocking, outside Tokio tasks. atm-daemon-client/src/lib.rs launch gate and publication polling are synchronous client APIs, with no production callers in the workspace. See randlee/sc-lint#82."
    }
  },
